LAYER: meta
PACKAGE NAME: openssl
PACKAGE VERSION: 3.2.3
CVE: CVE-2003-0078
CVE STATUS: Patched
CVE SUMMARY: ssl3_get_record in s3_pkt.c for OpenSSL before 0.9.7a and 0.9.6 before 0.9.6i does not perform a MAC computation if an incorrect block cipher padding is used, which causes an information leak (timing discrepancy) that may make it easier to launch cryptographic attacks that rely on distinguishing between padding and MAC verification errors, possibly leading to extraction of the original plaintext, aka the "Vaudenay timing attack."
CVSS v2 BASE SCORE: 5.0
CVSS v3 BASE SCORE: 0.0
CVSS v4 BASE SCORE: 0.0
VECTOR: NETWORK
VECTORSTRING: AV:N/AC:L/Au:N/C:P/I:N/A:N
