LAYER: meta
PACKAGE NAME: dbus
PACKAGE VERSION: 1.14.10
CVE: CVE-2019-12749
CVE STATUS: Patched
CVE SUMMARY: dbus before 1.10.28, 1.12.x before 1.12.16, and 1.13.x before 1.13.12, as used in DBusServer in Canonical Upstart in Ubuntu 14.04 (and in some, less common, uses of dbus-daemon), allows cookie spoofing because of symlink mishandling in the reference implementation of DBUS_COOKIE_SHA1 in the libdbus library. (This only affects the DBUS_COOKIE_SHA1 authentication mechanism.) A malicious client with write access to its own home directory could manipulate a ~/.dbus-keyrings symlink to cause a DBusServer with a different uid to read and write in unintended locations. In the worst case, this could result in the DBusServer reusing a cookie that is known to the malicious client, and treating that cookie as evidence that a subsequent client connection came from an attacker-chosen uid, allowing authentication bypass.
CVSS v2 BASE SCORE: 3.6
CVSS v3 BASE SCORE: 7.1
CVSS v4 BASE SCORE: 0.0
VECTOR: LOCAL
VECTORSTRING: AV:L/AC:L/Au:N/C:P/I:P/A:N
MORE INFORMATION: https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2019-12749

